## Control {{controlId}}: Authorize Remote Execution of Privileged Commands

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization authorizes remote execution of privileged commands and remote access to security-relevant information within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Remote privileged command execution is controlled through Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM) with time-bound elevation, approval workflows, and Conditional Access policies that enforce additional authentication for administrative operations.

{{#if pimConfigured}}
Privileged Identity Management requires explicit authorization before any remote execution of privileged commands. Administrators must request role activation through PIM, providing business justification for each elevation request. Activations are time-bound (maximum 8 hours) and require approval from a designated approver. All privileged command executions during active PIM sessions are logged and correlated with the activation request for audit trail completeness.
{{else}}
PIM approval workflows for privileged command execution have not been configured. Remote privileged access relies on persistent role assignments pending PIM implementation.
{{/if}}

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
Conditional Access policies enforce additional authentication requirements for remote privileged operations, including device compliance verification and phishing-resistant authentication methods across {{caPoliciesTotalCount}} configured policies.
{{/if}}

